  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of CPG meetings conducted in each quarter with defined agenda, meeting briefs and action plans</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">3 per quarter</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">(1) Eleven monthly CPG agendas
(2) Eleven monthly CPG summary notes produced containing political agreements on coordination
(3) Ten Work Stream updated overview agreed 
(4) Development effectiveness consultancy and work streams</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">(1)     11 monthly CPG meetings&#x2019; agendas and summary notes were prepared/delivered (At the November CPG plenary, members decided to skip December meeting and resume in January 2021). Results have included coordination and discussion on key issues, including: engagement with local businesses with reference to the Fact-Finding Mission (FFM) reports; travel authorization (TA) tracking; Reporting Framework for Allegations of Sexual Exploitation and Abuse; UN COVID-19 Country Preparedness and Response Plan (CPRP), the impact of COVID-19 on returning migrants; UN framework for the immediate socio-economic response to COVID-19 in Myanmar (UN-SERF); and the 2020 General Elections.

(2)     11 Work Stream updated overviews produced and circulated. CPG Work Streams have met regularly or on an ad-hoc basis and produced a range of outcomes. The Secretariat documented the outcomes on a monthly basis and presented the overview for monthly plenary discussion.

(3)     In order to enhance constructive and principled engagement with all stakeholders, including the Government of Myanmar and the international community, a 11-month consultancy, funded by the Italian Agency for Development Cooperation (AICS), was commissioned from February 2020 to January 2021 to support the Secretariat&#x2019;s day to day coordination/ communication work, and to maintain close working relationship with the Government, especially the Development Assistance Cooperation Unit (DACU) and the Foreign Economic Relations Department (FERD). Another 6-month consultancy, based in Nay Pyi Taw, was commissioned from November 2020 to May 2021 to accommodate COVID-related travel restrictions and support CPG coordination with the Government counterparts in the capital. 

(4)  CPs are currently supporting the restructuring process through the CPG Development Effectiveness Work Stream, the CSO/INGO Liaison Work Stream, and other sector-based coordination fora. Two meetings at the Development Effectiveness Work Stream and one meeting at the CSO/INGO Liaison Work Stream have been organized to discuss CPG engagement in the new coordination structure. The restructuring process is expected to conclude in early 2021.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1)	8-12 of CPG meetings conducted in each quarter with defined agenda, meeting briefs and action plans
2)	Existence and access (user base) to an expanded platform with updated data of cooperation
3)	Evidence like analytical briefs, discussion papers, concept notes on specific issues and themes are provided by the CPG Secretariat and external resource persons contributing to development debate and actions</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1)	Due to the challenging context in 2021, there was less motivation of the facilitators to convene monthly meetings. Towards the end of the year, with also new bilateral staff coming on board the request rose for frequent meetings, which were again scheduled on a monthly basis, including the agendas, meeting briefs and internal action plans for the FAs. Meetings were held in January, February, May, July, September, October and November, being 7 in total. 

2)	The CPG data was kept on the MIMU platform and accessible for the relevant stakeholders. It was however taken out of the public sphere due to privacy concerns seen the post-February context. 

3)	The CPG has played a pivotal role throughout the year in providing support on the development (and nexus) discussion, by proactively supporting the presentation and distribution of relevant analytical briefs, papers and joint reports. These include among others, the sharing of the World Bank Economic Monitor, the MIMU disability analysis and the draft Socio-Economic Resilience Response Plan. Towards the end of the year the new workstreams are starting to fall into place and thematic platforms are made available to share and discuss on civil society, economy, gender, governance and nexus.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
